      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors analyze the structure of acute abdominal pain in the general surgeon \"s practice. The article contains the results of an analysis of the frequency of various causes of pain, as well as a description of the most frequent causes of death in acute pancreatitis, cholecystitis, appendicitis, bleeding and perforative ulcer, ileus, strangulated hernia, and acute mesenterial ischemia."},
